#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variational Form and Ansatz {#variational-form-and-ansatz}"
msgstr "Bentuk Variasi dan Ansatz {#variational-form-and-ansatz}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To iteratively optimize from a reference state $|\\rho\\rangle$ to a target state $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$, we need to define a variational form $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ that represents a collection of parametrized states for our variational algorithm to explore:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengoptimumkan secara berulang daripada keadaan rujukan $|\\rho\\rangle$ ke keadaan sasaran $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$, kita perlu mentakrifkan bentuk variasi $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ yang mewakili koleksi keadaan berparameter untuk diteroka oleh algoritma variasi kita:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|0\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_R} U_R|0\\rangle\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|0\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_R} U_R|0\\rangle\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\rho\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_V(\\vec{\\theta})} U_A(\\vec{\\theta})|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\rho\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_V(\\vec{\\theta})} U_A(\\vec{\\theta})|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})U_R|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})U_R|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the parametrized state depends on both the reference state $|\\rho\\rangle$, which does not depend on any parameters, and the variational form $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$, which always depends on parameters. We refer to the combination of these two halves as an ansatz: $U_A(\\vec\\theta) := U_V(\\vec\\theta)U_R$.\n"
msgstr "Perlu diingat bahawa keadaan berparameter bergantung pada kedua-dua keadaan rujukan $|\\rho\\rangle$, yang tidak bergantung pada sebarang parameter, dan bentuk variasi $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$, yang sentiasa bergantung pada parameter. Kita merujuk kepada gabungan dua bahagian ini sebagai ansatz: $U_A(\\vec\\theta) := U_V(\\vec\\theta)U_R$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we construct our ansatz to represent a collection of parametrized states for our variational algorithm to explore, we realize an important issue: dimensionality. An $n$-qubit system (that is, Hilbert space) has a vast number of distinct quantum states in the configuration space. We would require an unwieldy number of parameters to fully explore it. Quantitatively, its dimensionality is $D = 2^{2n}$. To make matters worse, the runtime complexity of search algorithms, and others alike, grows exponentially with this dimensionality, a phenomenon often referred to in the literature as the curse of dimensionality.\n"
msgstr "Semasa kita membina ansatz untuk mewakili koleksi keadaan berparameter bagi algoritma variasi kita, kita menyedari satu isu penting: dimensi. Sistem $n$-Qubit (iaitu, ruang Hilbert) mempunyai bilangan keadaan kuantum yang sangat banyak dalam ruang konfigurasi. Kita memerlukan bilangan parameter yang sangat besar untuk menerokai keseluruhannya. Secara kuantitatif, dimensinya ialah $D = 2^{2n}$. Lebih teruk lagi, kerumitan masa operasi algoritma carian, dan yang seumpamanya, berkembang secara eksponen dengan dimensi ini, satu fenomena yang sering dirujuk dalam literatur sebagai kutukan dimensi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To counter this setback, it is common practice to impose some reasonable constraints on the variational form such that only the most relevant states are explored. Finding an efficient truncated ansatz is an active area of research, but we'll cover two common designs.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengatasi masalah ini, adalah amalan biasa untuk mengenakan beberapa kekangan yang munasabah pada bentuk variasi supaya hanya keadaan yang paling relevan sahaja diteroka. Mencari ansatz terpotong yang cekap adalah bidang penyelidikan yang aktif, tetapi kita akan membincangkan dua reka bentuk yang biasa digunakan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Heuristic ansaetze and trade-offs {#heuristic-ansaetze-and-trade-offs}"
msgstr "Heuristic ansaetze dan pertukaran {#heuristic-ansaetze-and-trade-offs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you do not have any information about your particular problem that can help restrict the dimensionality, you can try an arbitrary family of parameterized circuits with fewer than $2^{2n}$ parameters. However, there are some trade-offs to consider:\n"
msgstr "Jika kamu tidak mempunyai sebarang maklumat tentang masalah tertentu yang boleh membantu mengehadkan dimensi, kamu boleh mencuba satu keluarga litar berparameter sewenang-wenangnya dengan kurang daripada $2^{2n}$ parameter. Walau bagaimanapun, terdapat beberapa pertukaran yang perlu dipertimbangkan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Speed**: By reducing the search space, the algorithm can run faster.\n"
msgstr "**Kelajuan**: Dengan mengurangkan ruang carian, algoritma boleh berjalan lebih cepat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Accuracy**: Reducing the space could risk excluding the actual solution to the problem, leading to suboptimal solutions.\n"
msgstr "**Ketepatan**: Mengurangkan ruang boleh berisiko mengecualikan penyelesaian sebenar kepada masalah, yang membawa kepada penyelesaian yang tidak optimum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Noise**: Deeper circuits are affected by noise, so we need to experiment with our ansatz's connectivity, gates, and gate fidelity.\n"
msgstr "**Hingar**: Litar yang lebih dalam terjejas oleh hingar, jadi kita perlu bereksperimen dengan sambungan, gate-gate, dan kesetiaan gate ansatz kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a fundamental trade-off between quality (or even solvability) and speed: the more parameters, the more likely you are to find a precise result, but the longer it will take to run the algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Terdapat pertukaran asas antara kualiti (atau bahkan kebolehselesaian) dan kelajuan: lebih banyak parameter, lebih besar kemungkinan kamu akan menemui hasil yang tepat, tetapi lebih lama masa yang diperlukan untuk menjalankan algoritma.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "N-local circuits {#n-local-circuits}"
msgstr "Litar N-lokal {#n-local-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the most widely used examples of heuristic ansaetze is the [N-local circuits](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.NLocal), for a few reasons:\n"
msgstr "Salah satu contoh heuristic ansaetze yang paling banyak digunakan ialah [litar N-lokal](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.NLocal), atas beberapa sebab:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Efficient implementation**: The N-local ansatz is typically composed of simple, local gates that can be implemented efficiently on a quantum computer, using a small number of physical qubits. This makes it easier to construct and optimize quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr "**Pelaksanaan yang cekap**: Ansatz N-lokal biasanya terdiri daripada gate-gate lokal yang mudah dan boleh dilaksanakan dengan cekap pada komputer kuantum, menggunakan bilangan qubit fizikal yang kecil. Ini memudahkan pembinaan dan pengoptimuman litar kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Captures important correlations**: The N-local ansatz can capture important correlations between the qubits in a quantum system, even with a small number of gates. This is because the local gates can act on neighboring qubits and create entanglement between them, which can be important for simulating complex quantum systems.\n"
msgstr "**Menangkap korelasi penting**: Ansatz N-lokal boleh menangkap korelasi penting antara qubit-Qubit dalam sistem kuantum, walaupun dengan bilangan gate yang kecil. Ini kerana gate-gate lokal boleh bertindak pada qubit-Qubit bersebelahan dan mencipta keterikatan antara mereka, yang boleh menjadi penting untuk mensimulasikan sistem kuantum yang kompleks.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These circuits consist of rotation and entanglement layers that are repeated alternatively one or more times as follows:\n"
msgstr "Litar-litar ini terdiri daripada lapisan putaran dan lapisan keterikatan yang diulang secara berselang-seli satu atau lebih kali seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each layer is formed by gates of size at most $N$, where $N$ has to be lower than the number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "Setiap lapisan dibentuk oleh gate-gate bersaiz paling banyak $N$, di mana $N$ mesti lebih rendah daripada bilangan qubit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a rotation layer, the gates are stacked on top of each other. We can use standard rotation operations, such as [`RX`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RXGate) or [`CRZ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CRZGate).\n"
msgstr "Untuk lapisan putaran, gate-gate ditindih di atas antara satu sama lain. Kita boleh menggunakan operasi putaran standard, seperti [`RX`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RXGate) atau [`CRZ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CRZGate).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For an entanglement layer, we can use gates like [`Toffoli` gates](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CCXGate) or [`CX`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CXGate) with an entanglement strategy.\n"
msgstr "Untuk lapisan keterikatan, kita boleh menggunakan gate-gate seperti [gate `Toffoli`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CCXGate) atau [`CX`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CXGate) dengan strategi keterikatan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both types of layers can be parameterized or not, but at least one of them needs to contain parameters. Otherwise, without at least one parameter, there wouldn't be any variations!\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua jenis lapisan boleh berparameter atau tidak, tetapi sekurang-kurangnya satu daripadanya perlu mengandungi parameter. Jika tidak, tanpa sekurang-kurangnya satu parameter, tidak akan ada sebarang variasi!\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optionally, an extra rotation layer is added to the end of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Secara pilihan, lapisan putaran tambahan ditambah pada penghujung litar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, let's create a five-qubit [`NLocal`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.NLocal) circuit with rotation blocks formed by [`RX`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RXGate) and [`CRZ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CRZGate) gates, entanglement blocks formed by [`Toffoli` gates](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CCXGate) that act on qubits $[0,1,2]$, $[0,2,3]$, $[4,2,1]$ and $[3,1,0]$ and $2$ repetitions of each layer.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, mari kita cipta litar [`NLocal`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.NLocal) lima-Qubit dengan blok putaran yang dibentuk oleh gate-gate [`RX`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RXGate) dan [`CRZ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CRZGate), blok keterikatan yang dibentuk oleh [gate `Toffoli`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.CCXGate) yang bertindak pada qubit $[0,1,2]$, $[0,2,3]$, $[4,2,1]$ dan $[3,1,0]$ dan $2$ pengulangan bagi setiap lapisan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/c28d7b53-fbd7-42f5-a619-5a6b0b44e9fc-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/c28d7b53-fbd7-42f5-a619-5a6b0b44e9fc-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the above example, the largest gate is the Toffoli gate, which acts on three qubits, making the circuit $3$-local. The most commonly used type of $N$-local circuits are [$2$-local](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.TwoLocal) circuits with single-qubit rotation gates and $2$-qubit entanglement gates.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh di atas, gate terbesar ialah gate Toffoli, yang bertindak pada tiga qubit, menjadikan litar tersebut $3$-lokal. Jenis litar $N$-lokal yang paling kerap digunakan ialah litar [$2$-lokal](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.TwoLocal) dengan gate putaran satu-Qubit dan gate keterikatan $2$-Qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's create a $2$-local circuit using Qiskit's [`TwoLocal`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.TwoLocal) class. The syntax is the same as `NLocal`, but there are some differences. For instance, most gates, such as `RX`, `RZ`, and `CNOT`, can be passed as strings without importing the gates or creating a `Parameter` instance.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita cipta litar $2$-lokal menggunakan kelas [`TwoLocal`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.TwoLocal) Qiskit. Sintaksnya sama dengan `NLocal`, tetapi ada beberapa perbezaan. Contohnya, kebanyakan gate, seperti `RX`, `RZ`, dan `CNOT`, boleh dihantar sebagai rentetan tanpa mengimport gate-gate atau mencipta contoh `Parameter`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/c48521ee-db12-449e-af9f-7d8ec0fa7890-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/c48521ee-db12-449e-af9f-7d8ec0fa7890-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this case, we used the linear entanglement distribution, where each qubit is entangled with the next. To learn about other strategies, refer to the [`TwoLocal` documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.TwoLocal).\n"
msgstr "Dalam kes ini, kita menggunakan taburan keterikatan linear, di mana setiap qubit diikat dengan qubit seterusnya. Untuk mengetahui strategi lain, rujuk [dokumentasi `TwoLocal`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.TwoLocal).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Efficient SU2 {#efficient-su2}"
msgstr "Efficient SU2 {#efficient-su2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`efficient_su2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.EfficientSU2) is a hardware-efficient circuit that consists of layers of single-qubit operations spanning SU(2) and `CX` entanglements. This is a heuristic pattern that can be used to prepare trial wave functions for variational quantum algorithms or as a classification circuit for machine learning.\n"
msgstr "[`efficient_su2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.EfficientSU2) ialah litar yang cekap dari segi perkakasan yang terdiri daripada lapisan operasi satu-Qubit yang merentangi SU(2) dan keterikatan `CX`. Ini adalah corak heuristik yang boleh digunakan untuk menyediakan fungsi gelombang percubaan bagi algoritma kuantum variasi atau sebagai Circuit pengelasan untuk pembelajaran mesin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/5abc6f15-d7f5-466a-9659-78a11a2c5270-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/5abc6f15-d7f5-466a-9659-78a11a2c5270-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Problem-specific ansaetze {#problem-specific-ansaetze}"
msgstr "Ansaetze khusus masalah {#problem-specific-ansaetze}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While heuristic and hardware efficient ansaetze help us to solve a problem in a naive way, we can use problem-specific knowledge to restrict our circuit search space to a specific type. This will help us to gain speed without losing accuracy in our search process.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun heuristic ansaetze dan ansaetze cekap perkakasan membantu kita menyelesaikan masalah secara naif, kita boleh menggunakan pengetahuan khusus masalah untuk mengehadkan ruang carian litar kita kepada jenis tertentu. Ini akan membantu kita mendapatkan kelajuan tanpa kehilangan ketepatan dalam proses carian kita.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization {#optimization}"
msgstr "Pengoptimuman {#optimization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a max-cut problem, we want to partition nodes of a graph in a way that maximizes the number of edges between nodes in differing groups. The desired max-cut partition for the graph below is clear: the 0th-node on the left should be separated from the rest of the nodes on the right by a cut.\n"
msgstr "Dalam masalah max-cut, kita ingin membahagikan nod graf dengan cara yang memaksimumkan bilangan tepi antara nod dalam kumpulan yang berbeza. Pembahagian max-cut yang dikehendaki untuk graf di bawah adalah jelas: nod ke-0 di sebelah kiri harus dipisahkan dari baki nod di sebelah kanan oleh satu potongan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/ef9a5e1d-f70a-4f59-9112-2d8f71b253ba-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/ef9a5e1d-f70a-4f59-9112-2d8f71b253ba-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To utilize QAOA algorithm for a max-cut problem, we require a Pauli Hamiltonian that encodes the cost in a manner such that the minimum expectation value of the operator corresponds to the maximum number of edges between the nodes in two different groups.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menggunakan algoritma QAOA bagi masalah max-cut, kita memerlukan Hamiltonian Pauli yang mengekodkan kos sedemikian rupa sehingga nilai jangkaan minimum operator sepadan dengan bilangan maksimum tepi antara nod dalam dua kumpulan yang berbeza.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this simple example, the operator is a linear combination of terms with Z operators on nodes connected by an edge (recall that the 0th qubit is farthest right): $ZZII + IZZI + ZIIZ + IZIZ + IIZZ$. Once the operator is constructed, the ansatz for the QAOA algorithm can easily be built by using the `QAOAAnsatz` circuit from the Qiskit circuit library.\n"
msgstr "Untuk contoh mudah ini, operatornya ialah gabungan linear bagi sebutan dengan operator Z pada nod yang dihubungkan oleh tepi (ingat bahawa qubit ke-0 berada paling jauh ke kanan): $ZZII + IZZI + ZIIZ + IZIZ + IIZZ$. Setelah operator dibina, ansatz untuk algoritma QAOA boleh dengan mudah dibina menggunakan Circuit `QAOAAnsatz` dari perpustakaan Circuit Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/69599589-689e-4e0f-8135-937aedd9430d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/69599589-689e-4e0f-8135-937aedd9430d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous image illustrates the ansatz in basic gates for clarity. However, it can be expressed in multiple levels of decomposition by changing the `reps` argument or by drawing the circuit without the decompose method. For example, the following representation directly shows the QAOA structure with the default reps value, which is `reps=1`.\n"
msgstr "Imej sebelumnya menggambarkan ansatz dalam gate asas untuk kejelasan. Walau bagaimanapun, ia boleh dinyatakan dalam pelbagai peringkat penguraian dengan mengubah argumen `reps` atau dengan melukis litar tanpa kaedah decompose. Sebagai contoh, representasi berikut secara langsung menunjukkan struktur QAOA dengan nilai reps lalai, iaitu `reps=1`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/9724a36b-aae6-4d98-aad2-1090f0e1a941-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/9724a36b-aae6-4d98-aad2-1090f0e1a941-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Machine Learning {#quantum-machine-learning}"
msgstr "Pembelajaran Mesin Kuantum {#quantum-machine-learning}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In machine learning, a common application is the classification of data into two or more categories. This involves encoding a datapoint into a feature map that maps classical feature vectors into the quantum Hilbert space. Constructing quantum feature maps based on parameterized quantum circuits that are hard to simulate classically is an important step towards obtaining a potential advantage over classical machine learning approaches and is an active area of current research.\n"
msgstr "Dalam pembelajaran mesin, aplikasi yang biasa ialah pengelasan data ke dalam dua atau lebih kategori. Ini melibatkan pengekodkan titik data ke dalam peta ciri yang memetakan vektor ciri klasik ke dalam ruang Hilbert kuantum. Membina peta ciri kuantum berdasarkan litar kuantum berparameter yang sukar untuk disimulasikan secara klasik adalah langkah penting ke arah mendapatkan kelebihan potensial berbanding pendekatan pembelajaran mesin klasik dan merupakan bidang penyelidikan semasa yang aktif.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `zz_feature_map` can be used to create a parameterized circuit. We can pass in our data points to the feature map ($x$) and a separate variational form to pass in weights as parameters ($\\theta$).\n"
msgstr "`zz_feature_map` boleh digunakan untuk mencipta litar berparameter. Kita boleh memasukkan titik data kita ke dalam peta ciri ($x$) dan bentuk variasi berasingan untuk memasukkan pemberat sebagai parameter ($\\theta$).\n"

