msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/extracted-outputs/9d3a813b-40cf-4399-b912-714893987c30-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this lesson, you learned how to define your search space with a variational form:\n"
msgstr "Dengan pelajaran ini, kamu telah belajar cara mentakrifkan ruang carian kamu dengan bentuk variasi:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare states with a _parametrized_ quantum circuit, where gates are defined with tunable parameters\n"
msgstr "Sediakan keadaan dengan litar kuantum _berparameter_, di mana gate-gate ditakrifkan dengan parameter yang boleh dilaras\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to construct ansaetze that tradeoff speed vs accuracy\n"
msgstr "Cara membina ansaetze yang mengimbangi antara kelajuan dan ketepatan\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Heuristic ansaetze\n"
msgstr "Heuristic ansaetze\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Problem-specific ansaetze\n"
msgstr "Ansaetze khusus masalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our high-level variational workload looks as follows:\n"
msgstr "Beban kerja variasi peringkat tinggi kita kelihatan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A circuit diagram showing two unitaries: one preparing the reference state and another preparing the ansatz.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/ansatz-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambar rajah litar menunjukkan dua uniti: satu menyediakan keadaan rujukan dan satu lagi menyediakan ansatz.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/ansaetze-and-variational-forms/ansatz-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each variational parameter $\\vec\\theta$, a different quantum state will be produced. To find the optimal parameters, we need to define a problem-specific *cost function* to iteratively update our ansatz's parameters.\n"
msgstr "Bagi setiap parameter variasi $\\vec\\theta$, keadaan kuantum yang berbeza akan dihasilkan. Untuk mencari parameter yang optimum, kita perlu mentakrifkan *fungsi kos* khusus masalah untuk mengemas kini parameter ansatz kita secara berulang.\n"
